    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Find $AB$, if\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix and $B$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\cdot }_{\u2713}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}14 & \u2217 \\\\ \u2217 & \u2217\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\ & \\,14=6\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}14 & 11 \\\\ \u2217 & \u2217\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\ & \\,11=6\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 3 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}14 & 11 \\\\ 5 & \u2217\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\ & \\,5=1\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}14 & 11 \\\\ 5 & 8\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\ & \\,8=1\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$AB=\\begin{bmatrix}14 & 11 \\\\ 5 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.$",
