    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "If\n$E=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$F=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nthen $EF=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Here, $E$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix and $F$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $E$ and $4$ rows in $F,$ so $E$ and $F$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{E}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\cdot }_{\u2713}{F}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}={EF}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $EF,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}13 & \u2217 \\\\ \u2217 & \u2217\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\ & \\,13=5\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}13 & 10 \\\\ \u2217 & \u2217\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\ & \\,10=5\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}13 & 10 \\\\ 6 & \u2217\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\ & \\,6=1\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}13 & 10 \\\\ 6 & 8\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\ & \\,8=1\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$EF=\\begin{bmatrix}13 & 10 \\\\ 6 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.$",
